const pageTitle = "Paint, Stain & Exterior Finish Systems | Appalachian Sheds Inc.";
const pageDescription = "Exterior protection is a necessary finishing decision, not merely a color preference.";
---
<Base title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
<Fragment set:html={"<section class=\"article-hero\"><div class=\"shell\"><div class=\"breadcrumb\"><a href=\"/resources/\">Resource Center</a> / <a href=\"/options-upgrades/\">Options &amp; Upgrades</a> / 20</div><div class=\"eyebrow\">CUSTOMIZATION TOPIC 20 \u00b7 Structure &amp; Exterior</div><h1>Paint, Stain &amp; Exterior Finish Systems</h1><p>Exterior protection is a necessary finishing decision, not merely a color preference.</p></div><section class=\"asi-cost-review\" id=\"option-planning-prices\"><h2>Option pricing &amp; budget planning</h2><p class=\"asi-cost-alert\"><strong>Research-stage planning references:</strong> The figures below come from historical ASI planning material or approved model siding formulas. Historical amounts have NOT been verified as current Appalachian Sheds selling prices. They are not quotes. Final prices and any credits for included standard features must appear in a written proposal.</p><table class=\"asi-cost-list\"><thead><tr><th>Option / scope</th><th>Planning figure</th><th>Basis</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Standard exterior painting</td><td>$2.50\u2013$5.00</td><td>per exterior finish SF, historical</td></tr><tr><td>Two-tone painting</td><td>$3.25\u2013$6.50</td><td>per exterior finish SF, historical</td></tr><tr><td>Transparent/semi-transparent stain</td><td>$3.50\u2013$7.00</td><td>per exterior finish SF, historical</td></tr></tbody></table><p class=\"asi-cost-note\">Standard ASI building features remain included in the approved model price. Figures shown are for planning context only; these are not added to the online shed calculator. No site-specific price should be inferred from a price per linear or square foot.</p><a href=\"/options-gallery/\">Explore visual option comparisons</a></section><section class=\"asi-option-mini-gallery\"><h2>Visual comparison \u2014 planned photographs</h2><p>Images will be added where they help explain actual differences. No placeholder is represented as an installed product or completed ASI project.</p><div class=\"asi-mini-grid\"><div class=\"asi-small-slot\">PHOTO SLOT \u2022 Overall appearance</div><div class=\"asi-small-slot\">PHOTO SLOT \u2022 Close-up detail</div><div class=\"asi-small-slot\">PHOTO SLOT \u2022 Installed scale / context</div></div></section></section><div class=\"shell deep-layout\"><article><section class=\"deep-answer\" id=\"overview\"><div class=\"deep-eyebrow\">THE ESSENTIAL ANSWER</div><h2>What should you know before choosing?</h2><p>LP SmartSide and DuraTemp belong in a premium exterior paint conversation. Natural cedar and pine can support stain systems when the wood, exposure and maintenance expectations are appropriate. Factory-colored vinyl should normally remain factory-colored unless the exact product and proposed coating are specifically reviewed.</p><p>For Appalachian Sheds, the correct sequence is simple: select the siding \u2192 confirm the compatible coating system \u2192 prepare and protect the surface \u2192 then choose the color.</p></section><section class=\"deep-section\" id=\"topic-1\"><div class=\"deep-eyebrow\">PART 01</div><h2>The Finish System Is Determined by the Surface Underneath It.</h2><div class=\"deep-point\"><p>LP SmartSide and DuraTemp belong in a premium exterior paint conversation. Natural cedar and pine can support stain systems when the wood, exposure and maintenance expectations are appropriate. Factory-colored vinyl should normally remain factory-colored unless the exact product and proposed coating are specifically reviewed.</p><p>For Appalachian Sheds, the correct sequence is simple: select the siding \u2192 confirm the compatible coating system \u2192 prepare and protect the surface \u2192 then choose the color.</p></div><div class=\"deep-point\"><h3>One-Color Premium Paint</h3><p>Best for: LP SmartSide, DuraTemp and paint-ready trim where a clean, unified exterior is desired.</p></div><div class=\"deep-point\"><h3>Two-Color Paint Package</h3><p>Best for: body color plus trim, door or architectural accent.</p></div><div class=\"deep-point\"><h3>Solid-Color Wood Stain</h3><p>Best for: natural wood where higher pigment and stronger visual coverage are desired while retaining wood texture.</p></div></section><section class=\"deep-section\" id=\"topic-2\"><div class=\"deep-eyebrow\">PART 02</div><h2>Semi-Transparent Wood Stain</h2><div class=\"deep-point\"><p>Best for: cedar and pine where visible grain and warmer natural character are important.</p></div><div class=\"deep-point\"><h3>Transparent / Clear Wood Finish</h3><p>Best for: carefully selected natural-wood details where the homeowner accepts a closer maintenance cycle.</p></div><div class=\"deep-point\"><h3>Cedar / Natural-Wood Accent Finish</h3><p>Best for: brackets, shutters, flower boxes, porch details, gable accents and selected trim.</p></div><div class=\"deep-point\"><h3>Trim / Door Accent Finish</h3><p>Best for: one restrained accent color on doors, casing, fascia or architectural details.</p></div></section><section class=\"deep-section\" id=\"topic-3\"><div class=\"deep-eyebrow\">PART 03</div><h2>Recoat / Refresh</h2><div class=\"deep-point\"><p>Best for: future cleaning, prep, touch-up, caulk review, repainting or restaining.</p><p>Planning: site-specific; existing finish condition usually matters more than building age alone.</p></div><div class=\"deep-point\"><h3>Not Every Finish Belongs on Every Siding</h3><p>The coating must match the product underneath it. This is especially important with engineered wood and factory-colored vinyl, where manufacturer instructions should control the final finish decision.</p></div><div class=\"deep-point\"><h3>LP SmartSide Is a Paint Path \u2014 Not a Stain Path.</h3><p>Current LP application instructions call for a high-quality exterior paint and specifically say not to use stain on LP SmartSide products.</p></div><div class=\"deep-point\"><h3>A Premium Finish Starts Before the First Coat</h3><p>Paint and stain cannot compensate for wet material, exposed fibers, poorly prepared cuts, dirt, incompatible sealant or incorrect joint detailing.</p></div></section><section class=\"deep-section\" id=\"topic-4\"><div class=\"deep-eyebrow\">PART 04</div><h2>Clean, Dry, Compatible and Properly Detailed.</h2><div class=\"deep-point\"><p>Those four conditions matter more than choosing the most expensive coating.</p></div><div class=\"deep-point\"><h3>Surface Area + Trim Detail + Prep + Color Count</h3><p>Those four variables produce a more credible finish price than shed floor area alone.</p><p>These ranges are for planning. Final written pricing depends on actual finish surface, material compatibility, preparation, coating system and weather window.</p></div><div class=\"deep-point\"><h3>More Pigment Generally Means More Visual Coverage and Protection</h3><p>Exterior stain is not one product category. Transparent, semi-transparent, semi-solid and solid stains produce different appearances and different maintenance expectations.</p></div></section><section class=\"deep-section\" id=\"topic-5\"><div class=\"deep-eyebrow\">PART 05</div><h2>Visible Grain Comes With More Maintenance Responsibility.</h2><div class=\"deep-point\"><p>The more natural wood the customer wants to see, the more closely the finish condition should be monitored.</p></div><div class=\"deep-point\"><h3>Premium Color Design Is Usually Restrained</h3><p>For most Appalachian Sheds buildings, one body color plus one controlled trim or door accent will look more intentional than several competing colors.</p></div><div class=\"deep-point\"><h3>Siding \u2192 Roof \u2192 Trim \u2192 Doors / Windows \u2192 Accent Color</h3><p>Color should be the final coordination step, not the first design decision.</p><p>Use related body and trim colors when the shed should feel like a natural extension of the primary residence.</p></div></section><section class=\"deep-section\" id=\"topic-6\"><div class=\"deep-eyebrow\">PART 06</div><h2>Choose the Correct Finish System Before Choosing the Color</h2><div class=\"deep-point\"><p>Appalachian Sheds can coordinate siding, trim, doors, roof color, natural-wood accents, preparation, caulking and coating type so the final exterior looks intentional and has a maintenance path the homeowner understands.</p></div></section><section class=\"deep-section\" id=\"asi-scope\"><div class=\"deep-eyebrow\">IMPORTANT PROJECT DISTINCTION</div><h2>How this relates to an Appalachian Sheds project</h2><div class=\"deep-point\"><h3>Built on your property</h3><p>All Appalachian Sheds buildings are constructed on site. Property access, drainage, topography, location restrictions and the selected model can affect planning.</p></div><div class=\"deep-point\"><h3>Exterior shell versus finished interior</h3><p>Our standard building proposal describes a weather-tight exterior shell. Insulation, electrical, plumbing, heating, cooling, and interior wall or ceiling finishes are separate work unless expressly listed in the written scope.</p></div><div class=\"deep-point\"><h3>Only the written scope is authoritative</h3><p>Model-specific specifications, pricing, selected options, finishing requirements and any engineering or permit obligations must be confirmed for the actual building and site. Avoid treating this general guide as an engineering design or a permit determination.</p></div></section><section class=\"deep-section verified-planning\" id=\"verified-planning\"><div class=\"deep-eyebrow\">CURRENT PLANNING GUIDANCE</div><h2>Exterior finishing is a time-sensitive responsibility</h2><p>ASI exterior shells may include unfinished or factory-primed siding and natural unfinished cedar trim, depending on model and selected materials. Final painting or staining is optional and separately priced unless explicitly included.</p><p>ASI\u2019s current policy requires appropriate exterior painting or staining within 30 days. Roseburg also recommends an appropriate solid-color acrylic-latex finish on DuraTemp within 30 days of installation; follow the selected product and coating manufacturers\u2019 instructions.</p><p>Clarify who will finish the building, what surface preparation is included, and whether weather delays or site access affect the schedule.</p><p>Technical references: <a href=\"https://www.roseburg.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/DuraTemp_Install_081717-2.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Roseburg DuraTemp instructions</a></p></section><section class=\"deep-section\" id=\"next\"><div class=\"deep-eyebrow\">MAKE THE NEXT DECISION</div><h2>Your next planning step</h2><p>Review the exact siding/finish system, written maintenance responsibilities and manufacturer instructions alongside the proposed building specification.</p><div class=\"related\"><a href=\"/buildings/\">View Models &amp; Pricing</a><a href=\"/planning-guides/\">Explore Building Guides</a><a href=\"/options-upgrades/\">Browse Options &amp; Upgrades</a></div></section><section class=\"deep-section\" id=\"references\"><h2>Relevant planning references</h2><p>These official and manufacturer resources provide additional background. Product and jurisdiction requirements must be checked for the exact project.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.roseburg.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/DuraTemp_Install_081717-2.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Roseburg DuraTemp installation guidance</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.lpcorp.com/product-literature\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">LP SmartSide product-specific application instructions</a></p></section></article><aside class=\"deep-toc\"><strong>On this page</strong><a href=\"#verified-planning\">Current planning guidance</a><a href=\"#overview\">Essential answer</a><a href=\"#topic-1\">The Finish System Is Determined by the Surface Underneath It.</a><a href=\"#topic-2\">Semi-Transparent Wood Stain</a><a href=\"#topic-3\">Recoat / Refresh</a><a href=\"#topic-4\">Clean, Dry, Compatible and Properly Detailed.</a><a href=\"#topic-5\">Visible Grain Comes With More Maintenance Responsibility.</a><a href=\"#topic-6\">Choose the Correct Finish System Before Choosing the Color</a><a href=\"#asi-scope\">How this relates to an ASI project</a><a href=\"#references\">Planning references</a><a class=\"btn light\" href=\"/buildings/\">See Your Price</a></aside></div>"} />
</Base>

